---
import CaseLayout from '@components/CaseLayout.astro';
import ProcessFlow from '@components/ProcessFlow.astro';

const phases = [
  { label: 'Fetch', caption: '~60 feeds · 30h' },
  { label: 'Compose', caption: 'claude · forced tool' },
  { label: 'Ground', caption: 'cite or drop' },
  { label: 'Publish', caption: 'static · edge' },
];
---

<CaseLayout
  slug="il-primo"
  title="il primo"
  description="case study — a personal morning paper that builds itself every day: rss feeds grouped into cited stories by claude, with grounding checks in code, published as a static trilingual site."
  intro={[
    'Keeping up across world news, Europe, Italy, the Nordics, design and science means a lot of feeds, and most news apps are built for engagement, not for being done.',
    'Il Primo is one paper instead: built automatically every morning, aimed at a 20-minute read. Claude does the editing, and code checks every story before it ships.',
  ]}
  tech={['node.js', 'claude api', 'rss', 'github actions', 'cloudflare workers']}
  live="https://oggi.ilprimo.workers.dev"
>
  <h3 class="text-xs font-semibold text-[var(--color-cyan)] uppercase tracking-widest mb-4">{'// process'}</h3>
  <div class="mb-12">
    <ProcessFlow phases={phases} title="feeds to front page" />
  </div>

  <h3 class="text-xs font-semibold text-[var(--color-cyan)] uppercase tracking-widest mb-4">{'// what it does'}</h3>
  <ul class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-muted)] leading-relaxed mb-12 max-w-2xl space-y-2">
    <li><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] mr-2">→</span>reads ~60 outlets across eight sections and keeps the last 30 hours, de-duplicated</li>
    <li><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] mr-2">→</span>Claude groups items into stories through a forced tool call, so the output is structured JSON rather than prose</li>
    <li><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] mr-2">→</span>every story must cite feed items by id: unknown ids are stripped in code, and news with fewer than two outlets is dropped</li>
    <li><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] mr-2">→</span>sections run in order and are told what earlier ones covered, so nothing repeats</li>
    <li><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] mr-2">→</span>English source, translated to Italian and Swedish; a GitHub Actions cron builds it and Cloudflare serves it</li>
    <li><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] mr-2">→</span>no API key? it falls back to a headlines-only edition, so a morning never ships empty</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 class="text-xs font-semibold text-[var(--color-cyan)] uppercase tracking-widest mb-4">{'// outcome'}</h3>
  <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-muted)] leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
    A daily edition with an archive, built and published without anyone touching
    it. The design rule underneath: let the model edit, but never let it have the
    last word. Claude can't add a link that wasn't in a feed, and every story shows
    its sources so the reader can judge.
  </p>
</CaseLayout>
